  "id": "acquired-visual-impairment",
  "term": "acquired visual impairment",
  "definition": "Acquired visual impairment is reduced vision that develops after birth, and when it occurs early in life it can affect more than sight alone. In childhood, it may influence the development of motor, cognitive, social-emotional, and everyday functioning skills, with possible effects on autonomy, participation, and quality of life.",
